<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nogat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nogat is a distributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, about 62 kilometres long, which branches off the main river and flows north-east past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malbork">Malbork</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula-lagoon">Vistula Lagoon</a>. It bounded the land of the Prussian Pomesanians, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> built its chief castle, Marienburg, on its bank.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nogat.jpg" alt="Nogat" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DerHexer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nogat_river_and_Malbork_Castle_in_the_afternoon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
